ySlice<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read without hashing, and the hypergraph makes a constant number of allocations however many","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices it has. Every vertex-space read hashes its vertex once; index-space reads and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" algorithms hash none.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hyperedges can be appended but not removed. Equality ignores the order of the vertices and of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps from the vertices and the hyperedges to values can be attached (","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex map is read by vertex index or by vertex, an edge map by hyperedge position.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init()","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(hyperedges:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(vertices:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(vertices:hyperedges:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/degree(checked:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/incidentHyperedges(checked:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncide